course: dictionary
lesson: 12908
title: Long words for everyday things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Science and doctors often use long, formal words for everyday things. Eructation is one of them. «The doctor wrote the word eructation in her notes.» The word sounds serious, so the context tells you it is a medical or science word.
explain: Use the swap check to find its meaning. «Sam let out a loud eructation after the fizzy drink.» Now swap in a simpler word: «Sam let out a loud burp after the fizzy drink.» It still makes sense, so eructation means burp.
explain: At home, people say burp or belch. Eructation is the formal word for the same thing. Writers sometimes use it as a joke, because a long, fancy word for a burp sounds funny.
fact: Eructation is a noun. Its plural is eructations.
fact: «Eructation» means burping: air or gas from the stomach coming up and out through the mouth.
fact: «Eructation» is a formal, medical word. At home people say «burp» or «belch».
fact: Scientists link eructation to digestion, which is how the body breaks down food.
fact: Eructation is linked to fizzy drinks, and you may see the phrase «eructation after meals» in science books.
exercise: «Sam let out a loud eructation after the fizzy drink.» What does eructation mean? | *A burp | Sneezing | A yawn | Hiccups from being scared
exercise: The doctor wrote, «Eructation after meals is normal for some people.» Which word at home means the same as eructation? | *Burp | Whistle | Cough | Sneeze
exercise: Ella says eructation sounds like a joke. Why might a writer use it? | Because it means a happy song | *Because a long, fancy word for a burp sounds funny | Because it is a type of fish | Because it is the name of a castle
test: «The science book explained that eructation comes from the stomach.» What does eructation mean? | Feeling sleepy | A kind of cake | *Air or gas from the stomach coming up through the mouth | A loud cough
test: Which phrase uses the word in a sentence about meals? | Eructation under the bed | Eructation in the rain | Eructation before school | *Eructation after meals
exam: Which word means the same as eructation? | Yawn | *Burp | Snore | Sneeze
